01:15:52.380 --> 01:15:54.510 align:middle line:84%
The idea is we'll
say, well, actually,

01:15:54.510 --> 01:15:55.870 align:middle line:90%
we don't use the trapdoor.

01:15:55.870 --> 01:15:57.100 align:middle line:90%
But it's indistinguishable.

01:15:57.100 --> 01:15:57.840 align:middle line:84%
You don't know if
you're encrypted

01:15:57.840 --> 01:15:58.950 align:middle line:90%
zero, encrypted the trapdoor.

01:15:58.950 --> 01:16:00.250 align:middle line:84%
So we're going to
prove soundness,

01:16:00.250 --> 01:16:01.667 align:middle line:84%
assuming you encrypt
the trapdoor.

01:16:01.667 --> 01:16:03.640 align:middle line:84%
But in the scheme, won't
encrypt the trapdoor.

01:16:03.640 --> 01:16:05.250 align:middle line:84%
So then in the
scheme, the gamma is

01:16:05.250 --> 01:16:08.800 align:middle line:84%
going to be useless because
it won't correspond.

01:16:08.800 --> 01:16:09.640 align:middle line:90%
Yeah?

01:16:09.640 --> 01:16:11.570 align:middle line:90%
OK, great.

01:16:11.570 --> 01:16:13.730 align:middle line:84%
OK, great, great,
great questions.

01:16:13.730 --> 01:16:14.868 align:middle line:90%
So where are we?

01:16:14.868 --> 01:16:16.910 align:middle line:84%
So we said, here's the
Fiat-Shamir hash function.

01:16:16.910 --> 01:16:20.530 align:middle line:84%
The Fiat-Shamir hash function
will take actually an arbitrary

01:16:20.530 --> 01:16:22.233 align:middle line:90%
