01:17:26.620 --> 01:17:28.050 align:middle line:84%
And nobody's going
to decrypt it.

01:17:28.050 --> 01:17:30.340 align:middle line:84%
In the analysis, I'm going
to say, you know what?

01:17:30.340 --> 01:17:33.870 align:middle line:84%
I'm going to replace this
g with a very special g,

01:17:33.870 --> 01:17:39.600 align:middle line:84%
with a g whose encryption
is not beta bad.

01:17:39.600 --> 01:17:42.220 align:middle line:90%


01:17:42.220 --> 01:17:47.940 align:middle line:90%
But you're like, which g hat?

01:17:47.940 --> 01:17:49.520 align:middle line:90%
Which g hat?

01:17:49.520 --> 01:17:55.090 align:middle line:84%
How do we construct the g so
that we know that encryption

01:17:55.090 --> 01:17:58.680 align:middle line:90%
