description of this.

01:20:31.740 --> 01:20:33.490 align:middle line:84%
If you have two strings
and they're equal,

01:20:33.490 --> 01:20:35.580 align:middle line:84%
if you decrypt one, you
can apply decryption,

01:20:35.580 --> 01:20:36.705 align:middle line:90%
but they'll still be equal.

01:20:36.705 --> 01:20:39.040 align:middle line:84%
The decryption is just a
deterministic function.

01:20:39.040 --> 01:20:42.230 align:middle line:90%
So I guess.

01:20:42.230 --> 01:20:44.930 align:middle line:90%


01:20:44.930 --> 01:20:50.700 align:middle line:84%
For this g, I want
to argue that this,

01:20:50.700 --> 01:20:52.680 align:middle line:84%
which is Fiat-Shamir
hash function in alpha--

01:20:52.680 --> 01:20:54.950 align:middle line:84%
this is the Fiat-Shamir
hash function in alpha.

01:20:54.950 --> 01:20:58.370 align:middle line:90%
I want to argue this.

01:20:58.370 --> 01:21:01.100 align:middle line:84%
I want to argue,
if it was beta, I'm

01:21:01.100 --> 01:21:03.620 align:middle line:90%
going to get a contradiction.

01:21:03.620 --> 01:21:05.430 align:middle line:90%
I want to argue it's not beta.

01:21:05.430 --> 01:21:07.040 align:middle line:90%
Why?

01:21:07.040 --> 01:21:13.360 align:middle line:84%
If it was, then I can apply
decryption on both sides.

01:21:13.360 --> 01:21:15.430 align:middle line:84%
Then it means that
decryption of this

01:21:15.430 --> 01:21:19.840 align:middle line:84%
will be equal to
decryption of this.

01:21:19.840 --> 01:21:21.780 align:middle line:90%
Of course.

01:21:21.780 --> 01:21:23.150 align:middle line:90%
What is decryption of this?

01:21:23.150 --> 01:21:27.730 align:middle line:90%


01:21:27.730 --> 01:21:30.080 align:middle line:90%
g alpha.

01:21:30.080 --> 01:21:32.480 align:middle line:84%
So I just decrypt the
encryption of g alpha.

01:21:32.480 --> 01:21:33.280 align:middle line:90%
I get back g alpha.

01:21:33.280 --> 01:21:35.870 align:middle line:90%


01:21:35.870 --> 01:21:41.740 align:middle line:84%
But I know g alpha is not
the decryption of bad alpha.

01:21:41.740 --> 01:21:44.830 align:middle line:84%
Because g alpha is
the decryption--

01:21:44.830 --> 01:21:47.050 align:middle line:90%
not plus 1.

01:21:47.050 --> 01:21:48.060 align:middle line:90%
So it can't be.

01:21:48.060 --> 01:21:53.970 align:middle line:90%


01:21:53.970 --> 01:21:57.120 align:middle line:84%
So again, in the analysis-- so
let me maybe write this a bit

01:21:57.120 --> 01:21:58.080 align:middle line:90%
formally.

01:21:58.080 --> 01:22:00.860 align:middle line:90%
So let me write it up there.

